# =====================================================================
#  RTDA demo -- what git should never see
#
#  Three groups: stale trees kept on disk deliberately, build products,
#  and generated data. Nothing here is a source file.
# =====================================================================

# --- Stale trees, KEPT ON DISK ON PURPOSE ----------------------------
# These are full duplicates of live code plus their build output. Their
# *sources* were verified byte-identical to what is still tracked, so
# nothing unique is in them -- but they are 18 GB and deleting them is
# your call, not git's. Ignored, not removed.
#
#   aieml_float32/    15 GB   copy of archive/aieml/ + build tree
#   aieml_int16/      2.0 GB  ditto
#   aieml_batch_fp32/ 1.3 GB  fork of aie_batch/ from before the
#                             fp32/bf16 precision split
#   hls_projects/             hls4ml output; pl_fixed/ vendors what it
#                             needs, so this is historical now
#   hls_projects_bkp/         byte-identical snapshot of the above
#   data_backup14072026/      July snapshot of the fp32 weights, which
#                             are now tracked in model/weights_fp32/
#   data_batch_fp32/          MISNAMED: random int16, not fp32 weights
#   tmp_bkp/                  April notebook backups
#   hw_out_fp32/ hw_out_bf16/ byte-identical to results/aie_*/hw/
aieml_float32/
aieml_int16/
aieml_batch_fp32/
hls_projects/
hls_projects_bkp/
data_backup14072026/
data_batch_fp32/
tmp_bkp/
hw_out_fp32/
hw_out_bf16/
pkg_float/
pkg_int16/

# punit/ is the upstream model research tree. The pieces the build
# depends on are pinned into model/; these are large and local-only.
#   RealTimeAlignment/  601 MB, a duplicate of onnx_no-residual/
#   dsp_experiments/    1.3 GB, the alpha=0.1 vs 0.125 DSP sweep
#   hls4ml-tutorial/    2.1 GB, upstream tutorial, unrelated to RTDA
punit/RealTimeAlignment/
punit/dsp_experiments/
punit/hls4ml-tutorial/
punit/onnx_no-residual/checkpoints/
punit/onnx_no-residual/data/
punit/onnx_no-residual/Akshay/

